:question/math-academy-id "q-37290" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /3)}({tan}^{2}⁡(x)+3{cot}^{2}⁡(x)).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /3)}({tan}^{2}⁡(x)+3{cot}^{2}⁡(x)) & ={tan}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+3{cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}))}^{2}+3{(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =3+3(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =3+1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e37b91f0-ea0a-58b0-98d0-8f3626578dd6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "7a1f60af-0def-5ccf-b6e5-9b9a73c575fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "af1fac2c-3620-5983-b1bf-b23907d5f8e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "118c35c4-01b9-518d-b489-1e1bd00c5418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "ad57914d-3578-5cc1-839e-47970a85f5af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4f493888-cc2b-5ce9-aa9f-04a97d836676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "858e1d30-0d11-5afe-a048-c186050fe839" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47039/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer-field/choices ["q-47039/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-47039/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" "q-47039/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-47039/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-47039/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47039" :question/id #uuid "f27fcbd4-06f3-5af1-bede-4104ac6aed00" :question/math-academy-id "q-47039" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's attempt to evaluate the limit by direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x) & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.\n\nTherefore, to find the limit, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940317/assets/5e9d0e9d944cda9c97555ffdeac5aa245905f800cd99e11f5d172203bad3892d.png)\n\nAs $x$ approaches $\\pi $ from the left, the values of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)$ are negative and decrease without bound. Therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{-}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=-\\infty \n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $\\pi $ from the right, the values of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)$ are positive and grow without bound. Therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {\\pi }^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=\\infty \n$$\n\nSince the two limits are not equal, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e37b91f0-ea0a-58b0-98d0-8f3626578dd6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "9e0b4a1d-4f44-5b4a-b2eb-38de754147b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "585c0b10-46ae-5a20-a402-27cd258155af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "3bf61c50-2bb3-5aaa-86a4-e440fcf82502" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "12455579-bdb0-506c-8d9d-4b95448f5856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e286ceb9-23b7-5359-89ae-1eae4ae39369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "556fb9ed-ccb2-541d-9074-cd32681607a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65487/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-65487/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-65487/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-65487/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-65487/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-65487/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65487" :question/id #uuid "a3c895b3-cff7-5d1d-ad6c-1ae205543135" :question/math-academy-id "q-65487" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi }{csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=\\pi $ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }{csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b89b9224-71e0-5c90-8e9e-5fc3f7e29574"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-67609"] :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-344144/field-1/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744" :answer/id #uuid "87355fde-3a83-5901-b6ea-80f76125edb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344144/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f63c5db5-f691-540b-9e7a-8e469bf7467b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344144/field-1/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744" :answer-field/choices ["q-344144/field-1/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344144" :question/id #uuid "53d8dce8-397e-5b28-942d-ca10c6ec8958" :question/math-academy-id "q-344144" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{0}{1}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-344144/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e37b91f0-ea0a-58b0-98d0-8f3626578dd6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
